[h1]Changelog[/h1]

[h2][b][2.00] - 2026-09-??[/b][/h2]
[list]
[*] Added
[list]
[*] The [b]Protect Sector overview[/b] screen, opened from the right-click menu of a ship on the order or from its own icon in the top menu row: every fleet's statistics with a history of up to 48 hours, its state on the fleet coordinator, and its order settings including `Lost Ship Replacement`.
[*] `Fleet coordination`, on by default: the fleets on the order in one sector pick their targets together, matched to the size class of the enemy group, take on a group too strong for one fleet together, call for help and break off together. Its settings are on the overview's [b]Coordination[/b] tab.
[*] [b]Attack responses before a fleet's own targets[/b] option, on by default.
[*] `Problematic fleets`: a fleet that keeps refusing the coordinator's targets, or a ship without working weapons or ammunition, is marked and takes no targets until unmarked or able to fire again.
[*] The fire authorisation override from [b]Global Orders[/b] is respected.
[*] When a fleet leader is lost, the subordinate the game promotes takes over the order and the fleet's `Lost Ship Replacement`, at any time. This replaces the takeover added in `1.13`.
[*] When a target is gone, the next one is taken from the rest of its group first, then from the targets the subordinates fight.
[*] Every feature above is described in the README.
[/list]
[*] Changed
[list]
[*] The [b]Extension options[/b] page is built with `Options Helper`: the damage thresholds are sliders, and a [b]Debug Level[/b] dropdown (`None`, `Debug`, `Trace`) replaces `Enable debug log`. Old settings are carried over once.
[*] The debug log is reworked into compact lines only: [b]Debug[/b] carries the order settings and every state change, [b]Trace[/b] adds the reasons per candidate and per step.
[*] `Mod Support APIs`, [b]Options Helper[/b] and [b]Print Extension List[/b] are now required, so the minimum game version is `8.00`. For [b]7.50[/b] and [b]7.60[/b] use version `1.18`.
[*] Loading a save from an earlier version restarts the order once on every ship running it, with the same settings.
[*] [b]Share target with other[/b] is now `Share target with other fleets`.
[*] With both station attack modes selected, the experimental [b]Attack Station[/b] is kept.
[*] [b]Park on delay[/b] keeps the ship at its parking point while idle.
[*] The ship's [b]When attacked[/b] setting no longer interrupts an approach or an attack.
[*] A station left undestroyed is skipped for 30 minutes.
[/list]
[*] Fixed
[list]
[*] Idle ships re-scan their sector every few seconds again (broken since `1.13`), never stay idle for good, and no longer re-scan too often after an interrupted idle.
[*] An idle ship with station attacks no longer wakes every 30 seconds for a hostile build storage.
[*] Subordinates mimicking a commander use the commander's settings.
[*] Parking: the parking position is recognised as reached, a parked ship no longer drifts in a hazardous region, and a ship coming home arrives at its parking position.
[*] No more attack loops of an hour or more on a target the ship cannot see.
[*] No more hanging next to a target that docked or entered a highway.
[*] A ship chasing a large target closes in instead of flying up and down, and a repeated chase no longer gives up too early.
[*] The attack distance follows the ship's current radar range.
[*] A target lost from sight mid-attack is chased while still close, instead of being dropped at once.
[*] A target that left the home sector is never chosen.
[*] A fleet leader in a long fight checks its subordinates once, not once per attack.
[*] With [b]Aggressive subordinates[/b] on, subordinates are ordered to attack only once the leader attacks.
[*] With [b]Attack hostile only[/b] off, a non-hostile target turns hostile only to the ships attacking it, not to all your ships (game `9.00`).
[*] A ship without subordinates in the [b]Coordinate Attack[/b] mode now fires at the station.
[*] A ship stopped by a hazardous region stays stopped until the next hazard check.
[*] The "started" logbook entry is written once.
[*] Fewer script errors: after a load, in the experimental [b]Attack Station[/b] mode, in the station check, and for L or XL ships flying home.
[/list]
[/list]
[h2][b][1.18] - 2026-07-20[/b][/h2]
[list]
[*] Fixed
[list]
[*] Resetting subordinates order moved to an idle state, instead immediately after target is destroyed/lost/etc...
[/list]
[/list]
[h2][b][1.17] - 2026-07-15[/b][/h2]
[list]
[*] Fixed
[list]
[*] Fixed a bug where the ship (or fleet leader) could get stuck endlessly re-engaging a target that fled out of sensor range while still remaining in the sector, causing it to ignore other hostile threats (e.g. a nearby Kha'ak attack) until manually reset. The ship now correctly breaks off and searches for a new target once it can no longer detect the current one and it has moved beyond effective engagement distance.
[/list]
[/list]
[h2][b][1.16] - 2026-03-27[/b][/h2]
[list]
[*] Added
[list]
[*] New [b]Aggressive subordinates[/b] option to make subordinates more aggressive in attacking targets. It was introduced in version [b]1.13[/b] as the default behavior; with this update, it becomes optional and is disabled by default.
[/list]
[*] Fixed
[list]
[*] Fixed a bug with [b]Aggressive subordinates[/b] where subordinates were forced to attack targets outside the sector where the leader is.
[*] In some cases the [b]Park exactly there[/b] option was assumed by the game engine as a null value, which prevented the [b]Behavior tab[/b] from being opened on order failure.
[/list]
[/list]
[h2][b][1.15] - 2026-03-26[/b][/h2]
[list]
[*] Added
[list]
[*] New option [b]Received damage sensitivity[/b] to set the sensitivity of the reaction on receiving damage. There are three levels: 1 - low, 2 - medium, 3 - high. With different thresholds in idle or attack state.
[*] Possibility to set appropriate threshold for the sensitivity levels based on the percentage of the hull integrity per ship size and state in [b]Extension Options[/b] menu.
[*] New option [b]Ignore blacklists[/b] - to ignore blacklists when going to and protecting the `Home sector`. Equal to the behavior of the order before version `1.15`. Otherwise, when not set, the order will use [b]military[/b] blacklist group to reach and protect the `Home sector`.
[/list]
[*] Improved
[list]
[*] Behavior when hazardous or unreachable sectors are set as home ones. Order does not stop, but generates a failure instead.
[/list]
[*] Changed
[list]
[*] Due to the above change and specific behavior of UI with null values in order params, the default value for [b]Park exactly there[/b] is set to center of the sector instead of empty one. And now it does not make parking as default behavior but just sets the parking position to the center of the sector. Parking will happen only if [b]Park on delay[/b] is enabled.
[*] The [b]Park on delay[/b] is introduced instead of [b]Park at sector core[/b] to cover both parking in the center and parking in the desired position.
[*] Version is set to [b]1.15[/b] to be in line with the version of the main script of the mod.
[/list]
[*] Fixed
[list]
[*] Restocking and repairing now processes only reachable stations.
[/list]
[/list]
[h2][b][1.13] - 2026-03-14[/b][/h2]
[list]
[*] Fixed
[list]
[*] Avoidance of targets in some circumstances when the target is [b]L[/b] or [b]XL[/b] and the ship is [b]M[/b] or `S`.
[/list]
[*] Improved
[list]
[*] Implemented extra [b]push[/b] on subordinates to attack the desired target.
[*] Checking and sending ships to [b]repair[/b] for ships under this order's control and their subordinates.
[/list]
[*] Implemented
[list]
[*] Reassigning the order and its parameters in case the primary ship was destroyed and replaced by game mechanics. Previously, the order was just stopped in this case.
[/list]
[/list]
[h2][b][1.12] - 2026-01-30[/b][/h2]
[list]
[*] Fixed
[list]
[*] Order breaks attack "dangerous" enemy ships when [b]KUDA AI tweaks[/b] installed.
[/list]
[*] Improved
[list]
[*] Added [b]Protect Sector[/b] options menu in the [b]Extension Options[/b] if the [b]Mod Support APIs[/b] extension is installed.
[*] Added [b]Enable debug log[/b] option to log detailed information to the debug log.
[/list]
[/list]
[h2][b][1.11] - 2025-12-06[/b][/h2]
[list]
[*] Fixed
[list]
[*] Order ignoring new enemy stations in some rare cases.
[*] Error message generated by `DisengageHandler`.
[/list]
[*] Improved
[list]
[*] Improved the logic of resupply checks.
[*] Other small improvements and code cleanups.
[/list]
[/list]
[h2][b][1.10] - 2025-08-07[/b][/h2]
[list]
[*] Fixed
[list]
[*] Fixed possible incompatibility with [b]move_to[/b] command in the [b]X4: Foundations 8.00[/b] and upper.
[/list]
[*] Improved
[list]
[*] Targets handling in non-shared mode.
[/list]
[/list]
[h2][b][1.09] - 2025-05-18[/b][/h2]
[list]
[*] Fixed
[list]
[*] [b]Mimic[/b] mode not started correctly.
[/list]
[*] Changed
[list]
[*] If [b]experimental[/b] order of [b]Attack Station[/b] is selected but fleet has ships smaller than `L`- the both [b]experimental[/b] and [b]Attack Station[/b] options are disabled.
[/list]
[/list]
[h2][b][1.08] - 2025-05-11[/b][/h2]
[list]
[*] Added
[list]
[*] Internal (`experimental`) station attack order. Written from scratch positioning ships against stations, including reaction on stations drones attacks in non-OOS mode. Works only for fleets with [b]L[/b] and [b]XL[/b] ships. For only [b]L[/b] ships - four and more ships are recommended.
[*] Possibility to select station attack order - by default it is `Coordinate attack`. Other possibilities are [b]usual[/b] one and [b]experimental[/b] one.
[*] Additional confirmation for the working in hazardous regions, like `The Void`. Please be aware - the order will stop working in the sectors with the hazardous regions without the confirmation.
[*] Own icons for the [b]Protect Sector[/b] and [b]Station attack[/b] orders.
[/list]
[*] Improved
[list]
[*] Fully rewritten the logic of idling and scanning for enemy ships. Now it is more precise.
[*] Implemented workaround for the repairing/restocking ships. By default Player owned ships can be repaired only in current sector. Please be aware - after installing version [b]1.08[/b] the ships controlled by this order can go to be repaired/restocked after some time. It is not a bug, but a feature :-).
[/list]
[*] Fixed
[list]
[*] Fixed a reaction on attack on player's ships/stations by enemy drones.
[*] Accidentally attacks from the non-enemies are not considered as an attack on the player ships/stations.
[/list]
[/list]
[h2][b][1.07] - 2025-03-16[/b][/h2]
[list]
[*] Added
[list]
[*] [b]By negative relation[/b] to set the relation to possible targets more precisely.
[*] [b]Park exactly there[/b] to set the exact position where the ship should park when it is not targets to fight against. Useful for big sectors.
[/list]
[*] Improved
[list]
[*] Idle flying when any parking is not set.
[*] Attack of the stations via [b]Coordinate attack[/b] in now visible, as it is run not as a script, but as an order.
[/list]
[/list]
[h2][b][1.06] - 2025-03-01[/b][/h2]
[list]
[*] Fixed
[list]
[*] The Lost Ship Replacement not always works correctly.
[/list]
[/list]
[h2][b][1.05] - 2025-03-01[/b][/h2]
[list]
[*] Added
[list]
[*] Support for the [b]Lost Ship Replacement[/b] feature of version [b]7.50[/b]
[*] Added additional parameter to set a threshold from moving to target to attack it. In percentage of the radar range.
[/list]
[*] Fixed
[list]
[*] For version [b]7.50[/b] and higher, boosters are used always, despite the [b]Avoid boosters usage[/b] option.
[*] The default value for [b]Disable on destruction threat[/b] is [b]0 percent[/b] - i.e. disabled this check.
[/list]
[/list]
[h2][b][1.04] - 2024-12-31[/b][/h2]
[list]
[*] Fixed
[list]
[*] Slow floating to sector center when the "Park at sector core" is not enabled.
[/list]
[/list]
[h2][b][1.03] - 2024-12-26[/b][/h2]
[list]
[*] Added
[list]
[*] Added possibility to use the [b]Protect Sector[/b] order in the fleet mode with the [b]Mimic[/b] order.
[/list]
[*] Improved
[list]
[*] Improved the target separation in case of  "sharing" is disabled - variable wait is solve the problem with the same target selection.
[/list]
[/list]
[h2][b][1.02] - 2024-12-20[/b][/h2]
[list]
[*] Added
[list]
[*] Added parameter to set exact delay between scans.
[/list]
[*] Fixed
[list]
[*] Fixed a bug with approaching to the target - if it has equal speeds the catching is never happened.
[*] Added additional small delay in the approaching routine to prevent freezing
[/list]
[*] Improved
[list]
[*] Improved the experience gaining
[/list]
[/list]
[h2][b][1.01] - 2024-12-13[/b][/h2]
[list]
[*] Added
[list]
[*] Added option to protect ships and stations in the desired sector via reaction on attacks on them by hostile ships.
[*] Added option to record events to the logbook, including starts, travel to desired sector, flying to the target, attacking the target, destroying the target, etc.
[/list]
[*] Changed
[list]
[*] Between scans it uses [b]move.idle[/b] script.
[*] Changed the type of option to disable on destruction threat: from boolean to the percentage of hull to make this order disabled.
[/list]
[*] Improved
[list]
[*] Approaching to the target is rewritten.
[*] Attack of the ship is now under control of the [b]order.fight.attack.object[/b] script.
[/list]
[/list]
[h2][b][1.00] - 2024-12-06[/b][/h2]
[list]
[*] Added
[list]
[*] Initial release of the Protect Sector extension.
[*] Allows protection of a sector from hostile ships.
[*] Configuration options for home sector, attack stations, attack ships, attack farther from stations, attack only visible targets, attack only hostile targets, pursue fleeing targets, share target with other, preserve shield energy, and disable on destruction threat.
[*] Compatibility with X4: Foundations 7.1.
[/list]
[/list]